narrative:
## L2 Project: Build a Data Processing App

Put together everything you've learned — structs, enums, Vec, Map, Set, strings — to build a simple data processing application.

### Project: Student Grade Analyzer

Build a program that:
1. Stores students with names and scores using a struct
2. Uses a `Vec[Student]` to hold all records
3. Calculates statistics: average, min, max
4. Groups students by grade letter (A, B, C, F) using `Map`
5. Finds the top-performing student
6. Filters out failing students using `Set` of passing IDs

### Step 1: Define the Data Model

```xiom
pub type Student = {
  name: Str;
  score: Int;
} derive[Clone, Debug, Eq, Hash]

pub type GradeReport = {
  total: Int,
  average: Float64,
  highest: Str,
  lowest: Str,
}
```

### Step 2: Build the Analyzer

```xiom
fn analyze(students: &Vec[Student]) -> GradeReport {
  var total = 0;
  var max = 0;
  var min = 100;
  var top_name = "";
  var low_name = "";

  var i = 0;
  while i < students.len() {
    let s = &students[i];
    total = total + s.score;
    if s.score > max { max = s.score; top_name = s.name; }
    if s.score < min { min = s.score; low_name = s.name; }
    i = i + 1;
  }

  let avg = (total as Float64) / (students.len() as Float64);
  return GradeReport{
    total: total,
    average: avg,
    highest: top_name,
    lowest: low_name,
  };
}
```

### Step 3: Group by Grade

```xiom
fn group_by_grade(students: &Vec[Student]) -> Map[Str, Vec[Str]] {
  let groups = Map[Str, Vec[Str]]();
  var i = 0;
  while i < students.len() {
    let grade = score_to_grade(students[i].score);
    if !groups.contains(&grade) {
      groups.insert(grade, Vec[Str]());
    }
    // add student name to group
    i = i + 1;
  }
  return groups;
}
```

### Step 4: Find Failing Students

```xiom
fn find_failing(students: &Vec[Student], threshold: Int) -> Set[Str] {
  let failing = Set[Str]();
  for s in students {
    if s.score < threshold {
      failing.insert(s.name);
    }
  }
  return failing;
}
```

